+## Usage reported to `afterModelResponse`
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and the usage it receives covers the whole turn, so a deployer recording an audit entry, a billing line or a usage budget from it counts every provider call (re-cinq/HALEngine#93).
+
+- The usage handed to `afterModelResponse` is the per-turn total: the token counts of every provider call the orchestrator made in that turn, summed field by field, so a turn that ran two tool rounds reports all three provider calls rather than the last one alone ([validated by: reports the usage of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L69)).
+- A round whose provider reported no usage contributes nothing to the total rather than making it `undefined` or `NaN`: the rounds that reported are still summed, and a turn in which no round reported usage reports `undefined`, as it does today ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported usage when others reported none, and reports nothing when no round did](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly the usage of its single provider call, unchanged from before the total was introduced ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
